      "text": "Catalog Description"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "An introduction to finance including organization, taxes, capital markets, the commercial banking system, interest rates, financial analysis, financial forecasting, working capital management, marketable securities, accounts receivables, inventories, and short term credit instruments. Students will use Excel to apply concepts. "
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Prerequisite: ACC 175."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Learning Outcomes"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body Text",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "To gain an understanding of the key principles in finance and through practical problem solving learn to appreciate the link between theory and practice."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Teaching/Learning Strategies:"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "A lecture format will be used along with active Excel-based exercises in class. The student is expected to read assigned chapters before class."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading 1",
      "alignment": "LEFT (0)",
      "text": "Required Reading and Software"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Finance, Applications and Theory, Cornett vis McGraw Hill Connect"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Ability to use, save and upload Microsoft Excel files."
    },
    {
