    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Evaluation Methods"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Except in verified extreme problem cases, no make-ups will be permitted. In the event a make-up is permitted it must be taken no later than one week after the scheduled exam. Endicott College\u2019s official grading scale will be followed."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Grading"
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Each student will be assigned a letter grade as follows:"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Participation/Attendance: Attendance Policy: Students are required to abide by the Attendance Policy of Endicott College. "
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": " "
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Students are expected to attend every scheduled class and be prepared for class discussion. More than one unexcused absence will result in a reduction in attendance and participation grade. Six unexcused absences will result in a request for withdrawal."
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading 1",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Course Policies"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Academic Integrity Policy: Students are required to abide by the Academic Integrity Policy of Endicott College."
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "I take proper academic conduct seriously, as it is unfair to other students when cheating goes unpunished. It is important that the work assessed in this course is your own. Any plagiarism or cheating will result in a failing grade in the course, and all violations will be reported to the Dean of the Gerrish School of Business and to the Associate Dean for Academic Success. "
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Body",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Please consult with me prior to the start of week two if you are unclear about proper academic behavior and what constitutes misconduct, or if you do not know the difference between plagiarism and paraphrasing. "
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "AI Policy: Students are required to abide by the AI Policy of Endicott College, and violations are subject to the college\u2019s Academic Integrity Policy."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "The use of AI tools or software is prohibited, unless explicitly stated by the Professor. Lockdown Browser will be used for all quizzes and exams. Students are expected to have the proper software on their computers for Lockdown Browser functionality. "
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading 1",
      "alignment": "LEFT (0)",
      "text": "Turnitin Policy: By taking this course, students agree that all required assignments may be subject to submission for \u201csimilarity review\u201d to Turnitin.com, a tool intended to not just detect instances of plagiarism, but to prevent it as well. The tool is intended to help students identify passages that are unoriginal, incorrectly cited, or lacking appropriate source information. Submitted assignments may also be archived in the Turnitin.com database for the purpose of checking for possible future instances of plagiarism, additional similarity searches, and other educational purposes at the discretion of the instructor."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Student Support"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": " "
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading 1",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Accessibility Services "
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Endicott College provides equal educational opportunities for all students regardless of disability status.  If you believe that you qualify as a person with a disability as defined by Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA) of 1990 and its Amendment Act of 2008 (ADAAA), you are encouraged to register with the Center for Accessibility Services Office to request accommodations, auxiliary aides, and/or support.  The Center for Accessibility Services is located on the 2nd Floor of the Diane M. Halle Library. Please visit the Center for Accessibility Services website and you may contact Accessibility Services at access@endicott.edu with any questions.  "
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Heading 1",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Academic Support"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "The Division of Academic Success believes that every student can benefit from having a thought partner who supports their learning.  We offer innovative and individualized services that motivate you as you pursue your educational goals:"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Content and Writing Tutoring:  Work with content tutors who can help you understand, remember, and apply course content, or with writing tutors who will support your growth as writers and thinkers. Students can schedule free tutoring sessions on TutorTrac or stop by Halle Library 204."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Quick-Connect Coaching: Meet with a professional academic coach for thirty minutes to devise a solution to an immediate challenge, including unpacking a difficult assignment, creating a specific study schedule for an upcoming assessment, prioritizing multiple responsibilities, and more. Students can schedule free quick-connect sessions on TutorTrac or stop by Halle Library 204."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Academic Coaching: Grow your academic self-awareness and deepen your connection to your education by partnering once, twice, or three times a week with a professional academic coach to: develop and deepen academic confidence, resilience, and grit; develop time management and organizational systems and strategies; learn how to set and adjust goals; and recognize how to best utilize resources. This program has an additional cost. To enroll in academic coaching, students can email academiccoaching@endicott.edu."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Workshops: Our semester workshops help students build skills in crucial areas for learning and succeeding: time management, goal setting, note-taking strategies, and metacognition. See the website for a complete list of programs."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Title IX 2024 Policy: Institutions cannot discriminate based on a student's pregnancy or parental status; past or present, or any related conditions medical or otherwise. Qualified students may be eligible for academic adjustments enabling them to continue their academic process. For more information about Title IX Protections with regard to pregnancy or parental status, please contact Endicott's Title IX Officer, Christy Galatis at cgalatis@endicott.edu or at (978) 998-7746 and www.endicott.edu/title-ix"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Course Expectations"
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "For each credit hour students are expected to spend a minimum of two hours on work outside of class each week. For this three-credit course that means a minimum of six hours each week."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": " "
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Students must review the online Academic Calendar published by the Registrar\u2019s Office."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": " "
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Class attendance is expected of all students up to and including the last day of scheduled Finals in the semester. Students must plan accordingly."
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "style": "Normal",
      "alignment": "None",
      "text": "Topical Outline and Timeline"
    },
